   "source": [
    "## PART 1: Network preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective of this part of the lab is to practice using components and coreness to explore the meso-level structure of a social network and for filtering. Here you can use a retweet network you already generated. The first two tasks are short and specific: a warm-up, to see that you can compute these two types of meso-level structures. They are followed by a free explorative task, where you can make your own decisions about how to use these functions and in which order."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1bf68474",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "1bf68474"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Task 1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "Compute the components, print statistics about them (number, size of largest, ...), and mark the components in a node-link plot of the network (e.g. using different colours).\n",
    "\n",
    "#### TIPS\n",
    "\n",
    "- As for the previous lab, work on a filtered network so that the computations take a reasonable time on the machine that you are using.\n",
    "- The retweet network is directed, so you can compute both weak and strong components. Compare them."
   ]
  },
  {
