   "source": [
    "#### Notes / observations\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Three is one giant weak component that holds 5424/5648 accounts (96.0%). The other 224 components are one pair and 222 that are alone, which are probably active accounts whose retweet partners were removed by the strength ≥ 50 filter.\n",
    "\n",
    "The largest strong component has only 1500 accounts (26.6%), and 4011 of the 4060 strong components are alone. Retweets rarely go both ways, so only a core of accounts can reach each other in both directions. The rest are one-directional or retweeters.\n",
    "\n",
    "The giant weak component loses only 4% of the nodes, while the giant strong component would lose about 73%. The giant weak component is therefore the sensible one to keep."
   ]
  },
