      "source": [
        "#### Notes / observations\n",
        "\n",
        "The structures agree only moderately: the highest NMI is 0.56 (Infomap vs Walktrap), then Louvain res = 1.0 vs 3.0 (0.50) and Infomap vs Louvain at 1.0 and 3.0 (0.48 and 0.52). Louvain at res = 0.3 is the most different (0.12–0.24), except to Walktrap (0.34), and both have one giant community. This fits the visualisations: all methods agree on the hubs and their audiences, but they divide the dense mass of accounts differently, and in the plots this mass is drawn in a very small area, so the disagreement is hard to see. The numbers show it, because NMI uses all 5,424 accounts.\n",
        "\n",
        "NMI measures how much knowing an account’s community in one partition tells you about its community in the other. It runs from 0 (the two partitions are independent) to 1 (they are identical, apart from community labels). It’s a single number for the whole network. It doesn’t tell you where two partitions differ."
      ]
